I learn new details about nethack every day. Buck, XL 15
tourist with a passable AK, encountered a throne room one
level above the castle. The throne room contained two gray
dragons and other monsters of interest. Using his sleep
spell to immobilize selected monsters he managed to tame a
Olog-hai, get a whopping 3 HP from a nurse, eat one of the
two giants and get some gray scales from the two gray
dragons.

Buck had his blessed PYEC and a /oUT so when the two grays
didn't leave scales initially, he figured he would just
resurrect them until they did. Both grays, a black dragon
and several other monsters had met their end on the same
space, so Buck moved everything but the three dragons and
fired his /oUT.

Only one gray and the black were revived! Once these two
were dispatched again, this time the gray on the original
space and the black elsewhere, Buck zapped again, hopeful
this time the wand would bring back both grays. Only one
again. Well, Buck isn't quite as stupid as he looks in his
ODSM with the purple and green HS sticking out here and
there.

It must be that when two corpses of the same kind are on the
same space only one is resurrected! Sure enough, by
carefully managing WHERE he killed the gray dragons, he was
able to revive two at a time for the rest of this exercise.
All told, the gray dragons were killed 24 times. That seems
to line up with what Dylan told me last time this topic
(ZAP) arose.

Now Buck has a style issue. He had grown rather fond of his
ODSM. MR from the PYEC and Magicbane as a backup seemed safe
enough. Oh, well, at least now he has a choice.
